  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: We have only one data point (config_001: RNA-only, single-profile, PCA → 48.5% acc). The most critical unknown is whether the image modality carries any predictive signal at all; without this, we cannot rationally decide whether to invest remaining budget in multimodal fusion. Question: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) is the direct modality-counterpart to config_001, isolating the effect of switching from RNA to image features while keeping the profile setting (singleprofile) constant. This gives a clean, single-variable comparison. Why this is best: With 8 experiments left, establishing whether image features are informative is a prerequisite for any multimodal experiment to be worthwhile. If image accuracy is near chance, multimodal configs lose their rationale; if it is competitive or better, we gain a strong justification to explore fusion. Testing a different RNA encoder or multiprofile aggregation would be premature before we know whether the second modality is even useful."
}

